{"id":"module-2","locale":"en","nextCourse":"module-1","prevCourse":"module-1","title":"Module 2 — Kinematics","description":"Case Study, Lab, Homework. Velocity vs time, data table and live plot, acceleration from slope.","color":"#FF6F00","hero":"/content/module-2/hero.jpg","goals":0,"sections":[{"id":"background","title":"Background","url":"/course/module-2/background","steps":["background-1"],"goals":0,"duration":5},{"id":"data-lab","title":"Data Entry &amp; Live Plot","url":"/course/module-2/data-lab","steps":["data-table"],"goals":0,"duration":5},{"id":"analysis","title":"Analysis Questions","url":"/course/module-2/analysis","steps":["analysis-1"],"goals":0,"duration":5}],"steps":{"background-1":{"id":"background-1","title":"Background  ","html":"<x-step id=\"background-1\" goals=\"\"><p>In uniform acceleration, velocity and time are related by:</p><p><strong>v = v₀ + at</strong></p><p>where <strong>a</strong> is acceleration (the slope of a v-t graph) and <strong>v₀</strong> is the initial velocity (the y-intercept). In this lab you will enter your measurements and the graph will fit a straight line automatically.</p></x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"data-table":{"id":"data-table","title":"Data Table","html":"<x-step id=\"data-table\" goals=\"\"><p>Enter your (t, v) measurements in the table. The scatter plot and best-fit line will update as you type.</p><div class=\"lab-container\"><div class=\"data-panel\"><h3>Data Table</h3><table class=\"vt-table\"><thead><tr><th>Time t (s)</th><th>Velocity v (m/s)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t1\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v1\"></td></tr><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t2\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v2\"></td></tr><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t3\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v3\"></td></tr><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t4\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v4\"></td></tr><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t5\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v5\"></td></tr><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t6\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v6\"></td></tr><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t7\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v7\"></td></tr><tr><td><input class=\"t-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"t8\"></td><td><input class=\"v-val\" type=\"number\" step=\"0.1\" placeholder=\"v8\"></td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"results-box\" id=\"fit-results\"><p>Enter at least 2 data points to see the fit.</p></div></div><div class=\"plot-panel\"><svg id=\"vt-plot\" width=\"360\" height=\"360\"></svg></div></div></x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]},"analysis-1":{"id":"analysis-1","title":"Analysis  ","html":"<x-step id=\"analysis-1\" goals=\"\"><p>Based on your graph, answer the following:</p><ol> <li>What is the measured acceleration from the slope of your best-fit line?</li><li>Does your y-intercept make physical sense? What does it represent?</li><li>Estimate the uncertainty in your slope by considering how much the line could rotate and still pass through most of your data points.</li></ol> </x-step>","goals":[],"keywords":[]}},"availableLocales":["en"],"biosJSON":"{}","glossJSON":"{}","hintsJSON":"{}"}